{0 Native Lwt HTTP connections}

{!Httpkit_transport_lwt} drives {!Httpkit_engine} with native Lwt promises and unbuffered
Lwt_unix descriptors. {!Httpkit_transport_lwt.with_connection} cancels and joins its reader
and writer before closing an owned transport. No detached Lwt.async work is used.

One event loop owns a connection. One promise chain consumes incoming events.
Output admission is bounded; {!Httpkit_transport_lwt.collect_body} defaults to a 1 MiB cap.
{!Httpkit_transport_lwt.serve_connections} bounds admitted transports. The caller owns
listener creation, TLS, backlog, and routing. Custom transports must support
cancellation. Clock injection supports deterministic deadline tests.

The complete examples/runtime/lwt_example.ml uses the same pure handler as the
Eio example. Installed-package tests execute native and bytecode exchanges with
Eio unavailable.
